WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:07.600
Speaker 1: Republicans are now staging ridiculous
hearings in New York City on violent crime.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.360
These are Republicans from the House of Representatives.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.340
And you may say, David, wait a second.

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:16.180
House of Representatives, Washington, D.C.,
federal government.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:19.260
Why are they holding these hearings in New
York City?

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:24.570
The reason they are doing it is because they
are trying to run interference for Donald

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:30.529
Trump's indictment and arrest by attacking
Alvin Bragg with the idea.

00:00:30.529 --> 00:00:38.210
Why is Bragg going after Trump when Bragg
has violence in New York City to deal with?

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:42.690
Now, of course, you and I probably see that
and say, wait a second.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:45.340
Prosecutors can do multiple things at once.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:49.829
One of the problems we have in the United
States, which I've pointed out, is that there

00:00:49.829 --> 00:00:57.460
is too much focus on street crime rather than
corporate, financial and white collar crime.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:00.239
That doesn't mean we ignore violent crime.

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:07.790
It means that we have a system that at its
systemic structural level focuses on one type

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:09.610
of crime and not the other.

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:16.110
And that leads to a disproportionate focus
on wealthy people I'm sorry, not on wealthy

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:18.080
people, but rather on poor people.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:20.009
We've talked about this before.

00:01:20.009 --> 00:01:26.920
Low effort, low hanging fruit policing, for
example, makes it much easier to just go to

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:32.930
a poor neighborhood and, you know, harass
people, stop and frisk, etc., and not actually

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:38.720
partake in the other types of investigative
work that we should be seeing.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:41.340
So Alvin Bragg is doing nothing wrong.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:45.680
But Republicans want to make the case there's
violence in New York and Alvin Bragg is indicting

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.270
Trump for nonsense.

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:54.280
The other element to this is that we have
a red state murder problem and a red city

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.870
violent crime problem.

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:57.810
But Republicans don't want you to know that.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:01.890
They want you to believe, oh, it's liberal
cities that are dangerous and that's it.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:03.290
So let's take this from the top.

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:10.300
NBC News reports Trump Allies Take Fight to
brags Backyard with hearing on New York City

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.300
crime.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:15.569
The Manhattan district attorney prosecuting
Donald Trump highlights new police data that

00:02:15.569 --> 00:02:21.440
shows murders and under other violent crimes
have actually fallen in the borough since

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:22.440
last year.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:28.170
There's a picture on the screen of Republican
Congressman Jim Jordan because he is leading

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:31.580
this these series of hearings.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:37.519
As absurd as they are, the argument that Republicans
want to make is Democrats are weak on crime

00:02:37.519 --> 00:02:39.099
as it is.

00:02:39.099 --> 00:02:41.470
Blue cities have a crime problem.

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:46.849
And Alvin Bragg epitomizes this problem by
going after Trump rather than going after

00:02:46.849 --> 00:02:47.950
the violent crime.

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:51.150
Well, Eric Adams, the mayor of New York City,
was on MSNBC's.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:52.680
You see this morning.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:57.131
And he accurately and rightly pointed out
that not only is this a political stunt, but

00:02:57.131 --> 00:03:01.319
there is actually a bigger problem with violent
crime in many Republican cities.

00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:02.319
Here's Eric Adams.

00:03:02.319 --> 00:03:03.319
Speaker 2: Why?

00:03:03.319 --> 00:03:05.409
Let's bring in the mayor of New York City,
Eric Adams.

00:03:05.409 --> 00:03:10.150
By the way, what do you think of this field
hearing in your city about crime?

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:15.510
Speaker 3: I think is the highest level of
hypocrisy.

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:21.069
We know that cities all across America are
dealing with the issues around public safety,

00:03:21.069 --> 00:03:22.819
particularly the criminal justice system.

00:03:22.819 --> 00:03:24.480
And right in the largest city in Ohio.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:31.739
I was a reporter today, one of the tabloids
of the murders of over 50% in the first quarter.

00:03:31.739 --> 00:03:36.150
And so while crime is going down, homicides
are going down here, shoes are going down

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.150
here.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:40.099
Some of the major crimes, you're trending
in the right direction.

00:03:40.099 --> 00:03:41.819
So we system crime is going down.

00:03:41.819 --> 00:03:44.430
So I think come in here and highlight.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:47.299
And to brag is it's just really a political
stunt.

00:03:47.299 --> 00:03:49.510
Speaker 1: Now, is Eric Adams correct?

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:51.090
Yes, he is.

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:57.879
It is true that in New York City in 2022,
there was a violent crime rate, a homicide

00:03:57.879 --> 00:04:07.370
rate of 5.2 per 100,000 people, whereas in
Columbus, Ohio, there was a homicide rate

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:10.010
of 15.4 per 100,000 people.

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:16.769
The homicide rate in 2022 was nearly three
times higher in Columbus, Ohio, than it was

00:04:16.769 --> 00:04:18.130
in New York City.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:22.919
We've talked about both violent and property
crime rates being higher.

00:04:22.919 --> 00:04:30.830
In Oklahoma City, a red city in a red state,
then in New York City and New York state.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:34.860
And then there is also something, as I mentioned
earlier, called the red state murder problem

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:37.250
in 2020.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:44.700
Per capita murder rates were 40% higher in
states Trump won than in states Biden won

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:47.240
40% higher.

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:53.380
If you look at 2020, at the ten states with
the highest murder rates, eight of them voted

00:04:53.380 --> 00:05:00.770
for the presidential nominee from the Republican
Party in every election this century so far.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:07.470
Now, I don't want to do the thing that the
right does on so many different issues, whether

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:14.289
it's gas prices or debt and deficit and whatever,
and pretend that the entire crime story is

00:05:14.289 --> 00:05:19.650
just a matter of when Republicans are in charge,
it's more dangerous because that's actually

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:21.760
not so clearly the case.

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:26.590
And what I mean by that is crime is multidimensional
and very complicated.

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:29.810
Crime can be influenced by many different
factors.

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:33.199
It often also fluctuates from year to year.

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:38.680
When you look at crime, you have to look at
poverty inequality, which we know has a big

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:45.009
impact on crime, education levels, per capita
income, the relationship between political

00:05:45.009 --> 00:05:49.949
affiliation and crime rates is one element,
and it's not straightforward.

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:55.450
But the reason I bring all of this up to you
is that the right wing narrative of dangerous

00:05:55.450 --> 00:06:00.460
democratic cities or states or whatever, it's
absolutely and completely bogus.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.930
Now, I do want to give you one other.

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:05.800
I don't even know what this is.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:12.350
I want to advise you of one other way in which
this conversation is often mishandled by many.

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:16.620
There's a game that can be played, which is
you can say, Oh, you know what?

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:20.780
Red states are far more dangerous on average
than blue states.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:21.780
Okay.

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:24.520
So then Republicans will come in and say,
no, no, no, no, no.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:33.330
But the problem is, even within the red states,
most of the violence is in the blue cities.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:36.599
But then you can come back and say, well,
hold on a second.

00:06:36.599 --> 00:06:42.039
Just the fact that the violence is in the
cities doesn't really mean it's because of

00:06:42.039 --> 00:06:47.940
Democrats, because much of this policy is
set at the state level and the state legislature

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.930
and the state Senate are Republican.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:56.669
And then you can go back and say, well, within
the cities, the crime is mostly within the

00:06:56.669 --> 00:07:01.229
districts that are from Democratic city councilors.

00:07:01.229 --> 00:07:02.229
Okay.

00:07:02.229 --> 00:07:05.789
I think you get the point that this can be
sliced and diced a whole bunch of different

00:07:05.789 --> 00:07:06.789
ways.

00:07:06.789 --> 00:07:13.610
So my message here isn't to say it is because
of Republicans necessarily in every case that

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:15.819
violent crime and homicide and all these things
are higher.

00:07:15.819 --> 00:07:21.879
The point is the right wing story about crime
in Democrat cities, so-called, is completely

00:07:21.879 --> 00:07:23.009
and totally wrong.

00:07:23.009 --> 00:07:25.680
But what this is all about.

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:30.380
Is interference, running interference for
Trump and his indictment.

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:36.280
When Trump was arrested and indicted a week
and a half ago, the strategy was very clear.

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:40.090
What can Republicans in the House do to help
Donald Trump?

00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:44.470
And one of the things Jim Jordan has chosen
to do is to have these absurd hearings in

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:49.550
New York City rather than in Washington, DC,
where they should be in order to try to distract.

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:50.599
I don't think it'll work.

